  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following reaction.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0004_87816aee02d8.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 145px;\" /></p><p>On estimation of bromine in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>00</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> using Carius method, the amount of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgBr</mi></math> formed (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>) is____[Given: Atomic mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Br</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Ag</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>108</mn></math>]</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1.5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>PBr</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0004_bdce8fe31f17.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 161px;\" /></p><p>Number of moles in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi>gm</mi></math> of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>250</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>using Carius method all the Br will be converted into AgBr. So, using POAC method</p><p>Number of moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgBr</mi></math> formed from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>250</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgBr</mi></math> formed&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>188</mn></mrow><mn>250</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>gm</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
